---
const {kind} = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="support-figure">
{kind==='dependent' ? <>
<svg viewBox="0 0 680 280" role="img" aria-label="A 1 volt test source drives a port with a 2 kiloohm resistor to ground and a parallel dependent current source injecting 0.75 times Vt divided by 2 kiloohms upward into the port.">
<g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M90 108 V48 H450 V90 M450 170 V235 H90 V158 M265 48 V100 M265 165 V235"/><circle cx="90" cy="133" r="25"/><path d="M85 124 h10 m-5 -5 v10 m-5 15 h10"/><rect x="254" y="100" width="22" height="65"/><path d="M450 90 L478 130 L450 170 L422 130 Z M450 147 V113 m-5 7 l5 -7 l5 7"/><path d="M145 30 h50 m-7 -5 l7 5 l-7 5" stroke="var(--accent)"/><path d="M90 235 v12 m-14 0 h28 m-23 6 h18 m-12 6 h6"/><circle cx="265" cy="48" r="3" fill="var(--ink)"/><circle cx="265" cy="235" r="3" fill="var(--ink)"/></g>
<text x="135" y="119" class="symbol-label">Vₜ = 1 V</text><text x="149" y="19" class="output-label">Iₜ enters</text><text x="292" y="137" class="symbol-label">2 kΩ</text><text x="490" y="122" class="symbol-label">0.75 Vₜ / (2 kΩ)</text><text x="490" y="146" class="symbol-value">Dependent source</text><text x="330" y="30" class="output-label">Test port</text>
</svg><figcaption>Illustrative test circuit. The diamond denotes a dependent source; its arrow injects current into the port.</figcaption>
</> : kind==='incremental' ? <>
<svg viewBox="0 0 640 265" role="img" aria-label="Incremental circuit: a 10 millivolt signal source drives a 1 kiloohm series resistor and a 25.85 ohm diode small-signal resistance to ground. Voltage across the latter is 0.252 millivolts.">
<g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M90 103 V55 H245 M305 55 H430 V105 M430 170 V230 H90 V153"/><circle cx="90" cy="128" r="25"/><path d="M85 119 h10 m-5 -5 v10 m-5 15 h10"/><rect x="245" y="45" width="60" height="20"/><rect x="419" y="105" width="22" height="65"/><path d="M90 230 v10 m-14 0 h28 m-23 6 h18"/><circle cx="430" cy="55" r="3" fill="var(--accent)"/></g>
<text x="135" y="128" class="symbol-label">vₛ = 10 mV</text><text x="225" y="30" class="symbol-label">Rₛ = 1 kΩ</text><text x="460" y="133" class="symbol-label">r<tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="11">d</tspan> = 25.85 Ω</text><text x="452" y="77" class="output-label">v<tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="11">d</tspan> ≈ 0.252 mV</text>
</svg><figcaption>Illustrative incremental circuit at a 1 mA bias. The DC sources have been removed; every voltage and current here is a change.</figcaption>
</> : <>
<svg viewBox="0 0 660 285" role="img" aria-label="Thermal analogy: a heat input P feeds a temperature-rise node connected to ambient through thermal resistance and storing heat in thermal capacitance.">
<g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M90 108 V60 H480 V125 M480 143 V235 H90 V158 M290 60 V105 M290 170 V235"/><circle cx="90" cy="133" r="25"/><path d="M90 148 V118 m-5 7 l5 -7 l5 7"/><rect x="279" y="105" width="22" height="65"/><path d="M457 125 H503 M457 143 H503"/><circle cx="290" cy="60" r="3" fill="var(--accent)"/><circle cx="290" cy="235" r="3" fill="var(--ink)"/></g>
<text x="130" y="127" class="symbol-label">P / watts</text><text x="314" y="142" class="symbol-label">Rθ / °C/W</text><text x="520" y="142" class="symbol-label">Cθ / J/°C</text><text x="247" y="35" class="output-label">Temperature rise ΔT</text><text x="130" y="264" class="symbol-value">Ambient reference: ΔT = 0</text>
</svg><figcaption>A thermal analogy, not an electrical wiring diagram: heat flow acts like current, temperature rise like voltage, and stored thermal energy like capacitor charge.</figcaption>
</>}
</figure>

